		{"id":"d3fdf3d3a1ac7046","type":"text","text":"\n## **08:15** -\tReading \n## **08:40** - Reading C  **Exercises 17 - 21**\n## **08:55** - Homework \n","x":-324,"y":-133,"width":649,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2342817cc06f0ea4","type":"text","text":"# **Today's Class: Reading**","x":-301,"y":-234,"width":602,"height":68,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"37caefedc924698c","type":"text","text":"## 1. Before reading\n\n| Strategy                       | What to do                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 1. Predicting                  | Look at the title, pictures and headings. Predict what the text will be about. |\n| 2. Activating prior knowledge  | Think about what you already know about the topic.                             |\n| 3. Skimming                    | Read quickly to understand the general topic and main idea.                    |\n| 4. Reading the questions first | Identify what information you need to find in the text.                        |\n## 2. While reading\n\n|Strategy|What to do|\n|---|---|\n|5. Scanning|Look for specific information, such as names, dates, numbers or keywords.|\n|6. Finding the main idea|Identify the most important message of a paragraph or text.|\n|7. Finding supporting details|Look for examples, explanations and facts that support the main idea.|\n|8. Guessing meaning from context|Use surrounding words and sentences to understand unfamiliar vocabulary.|\n|9. Recognising signal words|Notice words such as because, however, although, first and finally.|\n|10. Recognising false friends|Be careful with English words that look like Dutch words but have different meanings, such as actual and eventually.|\n|11. Making inferences|Combine clues from the text to understand information that is not directly stated.|\n|12. Summarising|Explain the most important information in your own words.|","x":529,"y":-234,"width":884,"height":734,"color":"6"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}